---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Exclusions"
  description="Exclude gitignored files, semantic categories, and custom paths."
  current="/exclusions/"
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1>Exclusions</h1>
    <p>
      Exclusions describe files that no standard should measure. Use categories
      for semantic groups and paths for project-specific cases.
    </p>

    <pre><code>exclude:
  gitignored: true
  categories:
    - assets
    - configuration
    - documentation
    - generated
    - tests
    - vendored
    - dependencies
  paths:
    - src/generated/**</code></pre>

    <h2>Built-in categories</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Category</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>assets</code></td>
          <td>Static assets, images, fonts, PDFs, design files, audio, and video.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>configuration</code></td>
          <td>
            Tool and package configuration files whose shape is imposed by
            another system, such as package.json, tsconfig, go.mod, Cargo.toml,
            pyproject.toml, and .considered.yaml.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>documentation</code></td>
          <td>Repository prose such as README, changelog, docs directories, Markdown, text, reStructuredText, and AsciiDoc.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>generated</code></td>
          <td>Lockfiles, generated directories, codegen outputs, protobuf outputs, and generated filename suffixes.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>tests</code></td>
          <td>Conventional test files and directories from common language ecosystems and test runners.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>vendored</code></td>
          <td>Committed third-party source such as vendor, third_party, external, and vendored directories.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>dependencies</code></td>
          <td>Installed dependency directories such as node_modules, virtual environments, and package stores.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Paths</h2>
    <p>
      Custom paths use doublestar glob syntax. They are useful for local
      conventions that are meaningful to one repository but too specific for a
      built-in category.
    </p>

    <div class="note">
      <p>
        GitHub Actions workflows are intentionally not part of the
        <code>configuration</code> category. They are YAML, but they often behave
        more like operational programs than static tool settings.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
